            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="5gWmNrB">
                <source>description.ui_enable_reviews</source>
                <target>Lets visitors submit a review and displays the published ones. The moderation menu stays available either way. Leave to false until reviews are expected.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="HIIlbc1">
                <source>description.ui_map_google_api_key</source>
                <target>Only read when the provider above is Google. A browser key is necessarily published in the page a visitor loads: what protects it is the HTTP referrer restriction you set on it in the Google Cloud console, not this field hiding it here.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="ND.iLqC">
                <source>description.ui_map_provider</source>
                <target>Which service draws the maps a "Map" block places on a page. OpenStreetMap needs no key, no account and writes no cookie. Google needs an API key, a billing account, the visitor's consent before the map is drawn, and a Content-Security-Policy naming its hosts: without them the map stays a list of places and nothing says why.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="z8AyzGD">
                <source>description.ui_pdf_engine</source>
                <target>What draws the documents the site hands over as PDFs. “Automatic” uses WeasyPrint wherever it is installed on the server — the rendering is markedly better there — and otherwise falls back on the engine shipped with the bundle, which works everywhere. Pin an engine to have every environment produce exactly the same document.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="oJCCxE.">
                <source>description.ui_pdf_weasyprint_path</source>
                <target>Leave empty if the “weasyprint” command is found as it stands. On shared or managed hosting it is commonly installed in a Python environment of its own: state its full path then, for instance /home/clients/xxx/venv/bin/weasyprint.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="FX2LelG">
                <source>description.ui_pwa_android_fingerprint</source>
                <target>SHA-256 fingerprint of the Android app's signing key, as the Play Console shows it (App integrity); several separated by commas. Published in /.well-known/assetlinks.json with the package name</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id=".tcnyxU">
                <source>description.ui_pwa_android_package</source>
                <target>Package name of the Android app published on the Play Store, for example com.example.app; no linked app when empty</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="R5vo1zh">
                <source>description.ui_pwa_description</source>
                <target>One or two sentences saying what the app does, shown by Android in the install dialog next to the app screenshots (site graphics); 300 characters at most, none when empty</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="cJsJeMC">
                <source>description.ui_pwa_enabled</source>
                <target>Lets visitors install the site as an app on a phone or a computer, with a page shown when offline</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="RqrSOkt">
                <source>description.ui_pwa_share_target</source>
                <target>Path of the page receiving a link shared from the phone's Share menu (title, text and url parameters); none when empty</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="3QZWijd">
                <source>description.ui_pwa_short_name</source>
                <target>Name shown under the app icon, 12 characters at most; the site name when empty</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="RVA3kky">
                <source>description.ui_rating_icon</source>
                <target>The symbol visitors rate with: star, heart, thumb or smile</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="tuD18o0">
                <source>description.ui_rating_scale</source>
                <target>How many icons are offered. 1 turns the rating into a plain "like", showing how many voted instead of the average</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="tZ6fd2l">
                <source>description.ui_showcase_demo_url</source>
                <target>Url of the demonstration site the block showcase's examples lead to - their categories and sheets only exist there, left empty the examples are not clickable rather than leading to a page that does not exist</target>
            </trans-unit>
